Excel Features Used

- Power Query — data cleaning, extracting hour and day from timestamps
- Pivot Tables — multi-dimensional aggregation across store, category, time
- Slicers — interactive filtering by Month and Day
- Conditional Formatting — visual hierarchy in data tables
- Dual-axis charts — overlaying quantity and revenue trends
- Calculated KPI cards — dynamic metric display

---

## Key Takeaway for Business

Three stores. Similar revenue. But only one metric — 
**revenue per visitor** — reveals which location is truly 
punching above its weight. Data analysis isn't about 
reporting numbers. It's about asking the next question.

The Insight That Changes Everything
Most analyses rank stores by total revenue. When I calculated 
revenue per visitor, the story flipped completely:
> Lower Manhattan appears weakest in total sales ($2,30,057) —  
> but generates the **highest revenue per visitor at $4.81   
> making it the most operationally efficient location.

